---
import Layout from '../layouts/site.astro';
const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, '') + '/';
const docs = `${base}docs/`;
const commands = `pnpm add boundra zod
pnpm exec boundra init --name my-app
pnpm exec boundra create-domain order
pnpm exec boundra create-domain billing
pnpm exec boundra add-dependency billing/order
pnpm exec boundra check-boundaries`;
const tree = `domains/
  order/
    client/
    server/
    shared/
      public.ts
  billing/
    client/
    server/
    shared/`;
const contract = `import { defineQuery } from "boundra";
import { z } from "zod";

export const getOrderQuery = defineQuery({
  name: "get-order",
  input: z.object({ orderId: z.string().min(1) }),
  result: z.object({ orderId: z.string(), status: z.string() }),
});`;
const sections = [
  ['Getting started', 'Install Boundra and create your first domains.', 'user-guide/'],
  ['Boundary rules', 'Understand BR-001 through BR-006, public APIs and dependencies.', 'boundary-rules/'],
  ['Contracts', 'Define queries, mutations and routes, then connect your transport.', 'contract-schema-spec/'],
  ['Framework integration', 'Use Boundra alongside Vite or Next.js.', 'frameworks/'],
  ['Configuration', 'Configure domain discovery, paths, aliases and capabilities.', 'config-spec/'],
  ['Continuous integration', 'Run the checker before merge and require meaningful scan coverage.', 'ci-integration/'],
];
---
<Layout title="Boundra | Domain boundaries for TypeScript" description="Check TypeScript domain imports and validate application contracts with Boundra.">
  <div class="landing">
  <section class="hero shell">
    <div class="hero-copy">
      <p class="version">Architecture tooling for TypeScript</p>
      <h1>Keep domain boundaries <span>intact.</span></h1>
      <p class="lead">Catch invalid imports before they merge. Validate the contracts between your domains, without replacing your existing stack.</p>
      <div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href={`${docs}user-guide/`}>Get started <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a><a class="button secondary" href={docs}>Read documentation</a></div>
      <p class="requirements">Rust-powered CLI · TypeScript runtime · Node.js 20+</p>
    </div>
    <div class="boundary-preview">
      <div class="preview-header">
        <span>Boundary check</span>
        <span class="preview-file">billing → order</span>
      </div>
      <fieldset class="boundary-selector">
        <legend class="sr-only">Choose an illustrative import</legend>
        <label><input type="radio" name="boundary-example" value="blocked" checked /> Internal import</label>
        <label><input type="radio" name="boundary-example" value="allowed" /> Public API</label>
      </fieldset>
      <div class="example blocked">
        <div class="domain-map" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="domain-node"><span>billing</span><strong>server</strong></div>
          <div class="connection invalid"><span>×</span></div>
          <div class="domain-node restricted"><span>order</span><strong>server/internal</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="preview-path">domains/billing/server/invoice.ts</div>
        <pre><code><span class="syntax-keyword">import</span> {'{ orderService }'} <span class="syntax-keyword">from</span>{'\n'}  <span class="syntax-string">"@domains/order/server/internal"</span>;</code></pre>
        <div class="check-result rejected"><span class="result-icon" aria-hidden="true">×</span><div><strong>BR-004</strong><p>Cross-domain internal import. Use the target domain's public API.</p></div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="example allowed">
        <div class="domain-map" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="domain-node"><span>billing</span><strong>server</strong></div>
          <div class="connection valid"><span>→</span></div>
          <div class="domain-node exposed"><span>order</span><strong>shared/public</strong></div>
        </div>
        <div class="preview-path">domains/billing/server/invoice.ts</div>
        <pre><code><span class="syntax-keyword">import</span> {'{ getOrderQuery }'} <span class="syntax-keyword">from</span>{'\n'}  <span class="syntax-string">"@domains/order/shared/public"</span>;</code></pre>
        <div class="check-result accepted"><span class="result-icon" aria-hidden="true">✓</span><div><strong>Allowed by boundary rules</strong><p>Billing uses order's declared public API and dependency.</p></div></div>
      </div>
      <p class="preview-note">Illustrative rule example. Assumes billing declares order as a dependency; no CLI is running in your browser.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell content-section" id="quickstart">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2>Start with two domains.</h2><p>Keep your existing project. Declare one dependency, then run the checker.</p></div>
    <div class="walkthrough">
      <div><h3>Install and check</h3><p>The npm package includes a launcher for the native CLI. It downloads and verifies the matching platform binary on first use.</p><div class="code-panel"><div class="code-caption">Terminal</div><pre><code>{commands}</code></pre></div><a class="text-link" href={`${docs}cli-install/`}>Installation and supported platforms →</a></div>
      <div><h3>Declare the structure</h3><p>The CLI generates a manifest and layer directories. Billing can use order's public API because the dependency is declared.</p><div class="file-tree"><pre><code>{tree}</code></pre></div><a class="text-link" href={`${docs}domain-manifest-spec/`}>Domain manifest reference →</a></div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell content-section split-section">
    <div><h2>One contract. Both ends.</h2><p>Define the shape of a request and its result once. Boundra validates both ends of a call using your schemas.</p><p>Keep your existing backend and routing. Connect the runtime to a local transport or your own HTTP adapter.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${docs}user-guide/#4-implement-a-real-contract`}>Walk through a working contract →</a></div>
    <div class="code-panel"><div class="code-caption">domains/order/shared/contracts/get-order.ts</div><pre><code>{contract}</code></pre></div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell content-section split-section" id="ci">
    <div><h2>Make the boundary part of CI.</h2><p>Add a boundary check to your CI. The CLI produces machine-readable violations and returns a nonzero exit code when checks fail. Keep your typecheck and tests, and require meaningful scan coverage.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${docs}ci-integration/`}>CI configuration and exit codes →</a></div>
    <div class="code-panel"><div class="code-caption">Terminal</div><pre><code>pnpm exec boundra check-boundaries --format json</code></pre></div>
  </section>
  <section class="shell content-section" id="documentation">
    <div class="section-heading"><h2>Documentation</h2><p>Read the full guides and API references on this site.</p></div>
    <div class="doc-list">{sections.map(([title, description, href]) => <a href={`${docs}${href}`}><div><h3>{title}</h3><p>{description}</p></div><span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a>)}</div>
    <a class="text-link" href={docs}>View all documentation →</a>
  </section>
  <section class="shell content-section fit-section"><h2>Adopt it where boundaries matter.</h2><p>Use it when domain APIs and dependency directions need to be explicit. It does not replace authorization, routing, persistence, a bundler, or application tests.</p><a class="text-link" href={`${docs}product-positioning/`}>Compare adoption options and limitations →</a></section>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .landing {
    --landing-surface: #f8f7f5;
    --landing-border: #e3e0dc;
  }
  .landing .hero {
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(0, 1.12fr);
    gap: clamp(28px, 5vw, 70px);
    padding-block: clamp(54px, 7vw, 96px);
  }
  .landing .hero h1 {
    font-size: clamp(42px, 5.1vw, 76px);
    font-weight: 770;
    letter-spacing: -0.062em;
    line-height: 1.02;
    text-wrap: balance;
    margin-block: 16px 24px;
  }
  .hero h1 span { color: var(--brand); }
  .landing .version { color: var(--muted); font-weight: 600; margin-top: 0; }
  .landing .lead { font-size: clamp(17px, 1.55vw, 20px); }
  .landing .actions { margin-block: 30px 16px; }
  .boundary-preview {
    min-width: 0;
    background: #191918;
    color: #f5f5f4;
    border: 1px solid #383735;
    border-radius: 20px;
    padding: clamp(16px, 2.4vw, 26px);
    box-shadow: 0 20px 48px rgb(28 22 18 / 9%);
  }
  .preview-header {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    font-weight: 650;
    font-size: 15px;
  }
  .preview-file { color: #c4c0bb; font: 12px var(--mono); }
  .boundary-selector {
    display: flex;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    gap: 8px;
    margin: 18px 0 20px;
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    min-inline-size: 0;
  }
  .sr-only {
    position: absolute;
    width: 1px;
    height: 1px;
    overflow: hidden;
    clip-path: inset(50%);
    white-space: nowrap;
  }
  .boundary-selector label {
    display: inline-flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 8px;
    min-height: 40px;
    padding: 6px 10px;
    border: 1px solid #5e5b56;
    border-radius: 8px;
    color: #ddd9d5;
    font-size: 13px;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .boundary-selector label:has(:checked) {
    background: #39332d;
    border-color: #ffab72;
    color: #fff;
  }
  .boundary-selector label:focus-within { outline: 2px solid #ffd0a8; outline-offset: 3px; }
  .boundary-selector input { accent-color: #ff9b57; margin: 0; width: 16px; height: 16px; }
  .example.allowed { display: none; }
  .boundary-preview:has(input[value="allowed"]:checked) .example.blocked { display: none; }
  .boundary-preview:has(input[value="allowed"]:checked) .example.allowed { display: block; }
  .domain-map { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) minmax(26px, 0.25fr) minmax(0, 1fr); align-items: center; gap: 0; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .domain-node {
    border: 1px solid #5a5753;
    background: #252422;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 14px;
    min-width: 0;
    font-family: var(--mono);
    overflow-wrap: anywhere;
  }
  .domain-node span { font-size: 12px; color: #c4c0bb; display: block; }
  .domain-node strong { display: block; font-size: 13px; font-weight: 600; margin-top: 4px; }
  .domain-node.restricted { border-color: #e99482; }
  .domain-node.exposed { border-color: #8fcf9e; }
  .connection { position: relative; display: grid; place-items: center; min-width: 0; }
  .connection::before { content: ""; position: absolute; top: 50%; width: 100%; border-top: 1px dashed currentColor; }
  .connection span { position: relative; display: grid; place-items: center; width: 24px; height: 24px; border: 1px solid currentColor; background: #191918; border-radius: 50%; font: 17px/1 var(--mono); }
  .invalid { color: #f5a18e; }
  .valid { color: #98d9a7; }
  .preview-path { color: #c4c0bb; font: 12px/1.5 var(--mono); overflow-wrap: anywhere; border-bottom: 1px solid #44413e; padding: 10px 0; }
  .example pre { margin: 0; padding-block: 15px 18px; font: 12px/1.8 var(--mono); white-space: pre-wrap; overflow-wrap: anywhere; }
  .syntax-keyword { color: #d5b7ff; }
  .syntax-string { color: #ffd09e; }
  .check-result { min-height: 104px; display: flex; align-items: flex-start; gap: 10px; border: 1px solid; border-radius: 8px; padding: 12px; font-size: 13px; line-height: 1.5; }
  .check-result strong { font-family: var(--mono); font-size: 13px; }
  .check-result p { margin: 3px 0 0; }
  .result-icon { font: 19px/1.25 var(--mono); flex: 0 0 18px; text-align: center; }
  .rejected { color: #ffd0c5; border-color: #9c5144; background: #382521; }
  .accepted { color: #c3edca; border-color: #5a9564; background: #233629; }
  .preview-note { margin: 14px 0 0; color: #c4c0bb; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.55; }
  .landing .content-section { border-top: 1px solid var(--landing-border); padding-block: clamp(44px, 6vw, 78px); }
  .landing .content-section h2 { font-size: clamp(30px, 3.8vw, 46px); letter-spacing: -0.045em; }
  .landing .section-heading { margin-bottom: 32px; }
  .landing .code-panel, .landing .file-tree { background: var(--landing-surface); border-color: var(--landing-border); border-radius: 12px; }
  .landing .split-section { align-items: center; }
  .landing .doc-list a { min-height: 84px; }
  .landing .doc-list a:hover { text-decoration: none; }
  .landing .fit-section { padding-bottom: 80px; }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .landing .hero { grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr); gap: 32px; }
    .landing .hero h1 { max-width: 720px; }
  }
  @media (max-width: 370px) {
    .domain-node { padding: 10px 8px; }
    .domain-node strong { font-size: 12px; }
    .boundary-selector label { font-size: 12px; padding: 6px 8px; }
  }
</style>
